  "fee": "$375 (active physician, 2-year renewal) per the board FAQ, plus the Montana Prescription Drug Registry fee of $30/year ($60 for a two-year renewal) for physicians with prescribing authority. Inactive renewal: $190. Note: ARM 24.156.409 (rules PDF current through 3/31/24) itemizes the $190 inactive renewal but routes the active renewal fee to the department's standardized fee rule ARM 24.101.403; the $375 active figure comes from the board's own FAQ.",
  "lateFee": "100% of the renewal fee, in addition to the renewal fee (board renewal-process page: \"Renewal after a license's expiration date will automatically result in a 100% late fee, in addition to the renewal fee\"; ARM 24.101.403: late penalty is 100 percent of the renewal fee for each unrenewed renewal period). For an active physician that means roughly $375 penalty on top of the $375 renewal.",
