  "lapse": "No grace period. Per the DHHS renewal page: if you missed your renewal deadline, your license has expired and you cannot practice until it is reissued or reinstated; practicing after expiration incurs a $10 per day administrative penalty up to $1,000. Reinstatement requires the combined renewal + reinstatement fee, 50 Category 1 CE hours already completed within the 24 months before applying, and proof of ONE of the following within the 3 years preceding application: 1 year of active practice (any US state, DC, territory, or Canada), 1 year of approved GME, Board-approved CE, a Board-approved refresher course, or the special purposes examination. The Board of Medicine and Surgery does not routinely accept CE or the special purposes exam alone as evidence of continued competency absent recent practice; under Neb. Rev. Stat. 38-2026.01, a physician who has not actively practiced for the 2 years preceding application may be offered only a reentry license, and declining the reentry license results in denial of the application. A reinstated license expires on the same October 1 of the next even-numbered year.",
