  "lapse": "30-day grace period by statute (N.J.S.A. 45:1-7.1(b)): the license may be renewed within 30 days after expiration by paying the renewal fee plus late fee, and during those 30 days the license remains valid and the physician is not deemed practicing without a license. Any license not renewed within 30 days of expiration is SUSPENDED without a hearing, and continued practice after the 30 days is unlicensed practice even if no suspension notice was received (45:1-7.1(c)). Reinstatement (N.J.S.A. 45:1-7.4; request application via BMEReinstatement@dca.njoag.gov) requires: renewal application, certification of employment for every job held during suspension, the current biennial renewal fee, the unpaid back renewal fee, a $175 reinstatement fee, and proof of the CME that was due (board presentation adds a criminal history background check). A current out-of-state license in good standing with that state's CE satisfied can substitute for the CME proof. The board may require an examination, skills assessment, or refresher course if it suspects practice deficiencies.",
