  "processing": "Per the MD board licensing FAQ (written for the legacy process): renewals are posted daily as received and wallet cards are printed and mailed each Monday for everyone who renewed the previous week; initial license applications average 6 to 8 weeks. No processing-time commitment is published for the new 2026 portal.",
  "lapse": "MD: no grace period (\"No grace period beyond that provided by law shall be allowed,\" OAC 435:10-7-10). A license inactive more than 60 days requires the full reinstatement process (board licensing FAQ, reinstatement fee $500). By statute 59 O.S. 495d, failure to reregister within 60 days after the registration period ends suspends the license, the Board notifies the district attorney, and reinstatement requires meeting current initial-licensure standards plus possible clinical competency examination unless at least 50 percent of monthly activity during the lapse was medical practice. Practicing without a current renewal is a misdemeanor with a fine of at least $1,000 and grounds for revocation (59 O.S. 495b). DO: renewal with $150 late fee allowed July 1 to August 31; after cancellation a $500 reinstatement fee applies (within 2 years of cancellation) in addition to other fees.",
