  "due": "Fixed quarterly dates assigned by TMB at licensure. Board text: \"Physician licenses expire at one of 4 times during the year; February 28th, May 31st, August 31st, or November 30th.\" The year is set by license-number parity: \"Even number licenses expire in even number years and odd number licenses expire in odd number years.\" Initial registration is pro-rated (12-month $281.48 or 24-month $467.48) to land the license on its assigned cycle.",
  "fee": "$491.48 (biennial physician registration, as of 9/1/2025): Agency fee $370.00 + SB 104 fee $80.00 + Office of Patient Protection $2.00 + NPDB $21.00 + Texas Physician Health Program $7.00 + PMP $11.48. Paper renewal adds a $50 surcharge when online renewal is available; credit card payment adds a Texas.gov processing fee (electronic check does not).",
