  "due": "MD: \"Physician licenses expire on January 31 of even years.\" DO: \"Osteopathic Physician and Surgeon license renewals are due May 31st of even years.\" Controlled substance licenses renew at the same time as the main license. (Next renewal for both: 2028, since the 2026 dates have passed.)",
  "fee": "$193 (MD or DO, 2-year renewal). Add $78 to renew a Utah controlled substance license (total $271). Verified on the FY 7/1/2025-6/30/2026 DOPL fee schedule (\"Physician and Surgeon ... Renewal Fee 193.00\"; \"Osteopathic Physician and Surgeon 200.00 / 193.00\"; \"Controlled Substance 100.00 / 78.00\") and stated as \"$193 renewal fee\" on the DO renewal page. Fees are non-refundable and \"subject to change each July 1.\"",
  "lateFee": "No separate late-renewal window; a lapsed license is a reinstatement. Within 30 days after expiration: renewal fee PLUS $20 for EACH license being reinstated. After 30 days and within 2 years: renewal fee PLUS $50 for EACH license (from the DOPL Renewal/Reinstatement form v.20231107; matches the fee schedule's \"Late Renewal Fee $20.00 / Reinstatement Fee $50.00\"). The physician license and the controlled substance license are separate licenses, so the per-license fee applies to each.",
  "processing": "Online renewal via My License One: payment receipt emailed within 2 business days; a copy of the renewed license is emailed 1-3 business days after approval (stated on the DO renewal page; both professions use the same My License One system). No published timeline for paper reinstatements.",
  "lapse": "No grace period: under Utah Code 58-1-308(2)(b) \"A license that is not renewed prior to the expiration date shown on the license automatically expires.\" Reinstatement is available within 2 years of nonrenewal (renewal fee + reinstatement fee + proof of renewal qualifications); a license \"reinstated no later than 120 days after it expires shall be retroactively reinstated to the date it expired\" (58-1-308(5)(c)). After 2 years you must qualify for a new license (58-1-308(6)(a)), with a 6-month exception for those practicing under federal employment or another state license after reestablishing Utah domicile. Reinstatement cannot be done online; DOPL requires the manual Renewal/Reinstatement form. Practicing after expiration is unlawful conduct and a criminal offense (Utah Code 58-1-501(1)(a), 58-1-502), and DOPL may discipline for time worked unlicensed even after reinstatement.",
