  "lapse": "No practice grace period: the license expires October 31 if no renewal was filed. However, under Wis. Stat. 227.51(2) (quoted on the DSPS physician page), if the renewal application and fee are submitted by 11:59 pm on the deadline, the existing license remains valid until DSPS finishes acting on the application. After expiration, the credential can be restored at any time by paying the renewal fee plus the $25 late fee (Wis. Stat. 440.08(3)(a)). If expired more than 5 years, the board may impose additional restoration requirements to establish competency, not to exceed initial-licensure education/exam requirements (Wis. Stat. 440.08(3)(b)). DSPS may also summarily deny a renewal to protect public health, safety, or welfare, with a 30-day window to request a hearing (Wis. Stat. 440.08(4)).",
